--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,5 +5,27 @@ A small expense ledger. Entries live in a JSON file (`--data` or `$LEDGER_DATA`)
     python -m ledger add 2026-01-05 12.50 food "lunch"
     python -m ledger list
     python -m ledger report --by month
+    python -m ledger export --format csv
+    python -m ledger --data expenses.json export --format json --output entries.json
+
+`export` requires `--format csv` or `--format json`. It exports individual entries
+in ascending date order, preserving source order for entries on the same date.
+Both formats contain `date`, `amount`, `category`, and `note` as text; amounts
+have two decimal places, including negative refunds (for example, `-3.00`).
+CSV includes the header `date,amount,category,note` and quotes text as needed.
+JSON has the shape `{"version":1,"entries":[{"date":"2026-01-05","amount":"12.50","category":"food","note":"lunch"}]}`.
+An empty ledger produces a CSV header or a JSON object with an empty `entries` array.
+
+Exports go to standard output unless `--output FILE` is supplied. File exports
+print nothing to standard output. Existing files are preserved unless `--force`
+is supplied, for example:
+
+    python -m ledger export --format csv --output entries.csv --force
+
+Missing or unsupported formats, existing destinations without `--force`, and
+unwritable output paths return status 2 with a one-line error on standard error.
+Successful exports return status 0. All commands select the data file using
+the global `--data` option first, then `$LEDGER_DATA`, then `ledger.json`.
+A missing data file is treated as an empty ledger.
 
 Tests: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
